course: dictionary
lesson: 6816
title: Words for people who help us
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You do not need to know every word to understand a text. When you meet a new word, read the words around it, because they are its context and often leave clues. «A squint, or strabismus, is when the eyes don't line up, and orthoptists, eye workers who help with squints and lazy eyes, may suggest glasses, patches or an operation.»
explain: The words between the commas, eye workers who help with squints and lazy eyes, explain what an orthoptist is. So an orthoptist is a person who works with eyes. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «...and eye workers who help with squints and lazy eyes, may suggest glasses...» It still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Some words are about jobs, and the sentence often tells you what the person does. Here an orthoptist checks and treats eye problems. If the clues are not enough, a dictionary will give you the exact meaning.
fact: An orthoptist is a health professional who checks and treats problems with how the eyes move and work together.
fact: «Squint» means the eyes don't line up. It is also called strabismus.
fact: «Lazy eye» is a problem where one eye does not see as well as it should.
fact: Orthoptists may suggest glasses, eye patches or an operation to help these problems.
fact: Children may see an orthoptist at an eye clinic.
exercise: What is an orthoptist? | A teacher who helps children learn to read | *A health professional who checks and treats problems with how the eyes move and work together | A person who sells sunglasses in a shop | A nurse who takes care of teeth
exercise: «A squint, or strabismus, is when the eyes don't line up.» Find and copy the word that means the same as strabismus. | glasses | operation | orthoptists | *squint
exercise: A child's eyes do not work well together. What might an orthoptist suggest? | *Glasses or an eye patch | A bigger school bag | A new bicycle | A holiday by the sea
test: Mia's eyes don't line up, so she sees an orthoptist at the eye clinic. What is an orthoptist? | *An eye worker who helps with squints and lazy eyes | A driver who takes people to the clinic | A shop worker who sells sweets | A teacher of maths
test: Which word means the same as strabismus in this sentence: «A squint, or strabismus, is when the eyes don't line up»? | lazy eye | *squint | patch | operation
exam: Read: «An orthoptist may suggest a patch for a lazy eye.» What does lazy eye mean? | *An eye that does not see as well as it should | A pair of glasses with a broken frame | An eye that is painted for a party | An eye that is closed for a long sleep
